title: 'pvf: avoid leaking job pipes on PoV decompression failures'
doc:
  - audience: [Node Dev, Node Operator]
    description: |
      Allocate execution job pipes only after PoV decompression succeeds, so
      repeated malformed PoVs cannot exhaust file descriptors in a reused
      execution worker. No API changes or storage migration are required.
crates:
  - name: polkadot-node-core-pvf-execute-worker
    bump: patch
  - name: polkadot-node-core-pvf
    bump: none
